# Upload filter for `gcloud run deploy --source .` (Cloud Build staging tarball).
#
# This is NOT redundant with .dockerignore, and the two run at different points:
#   .gcloudignore  — what gcloud uploads to the Cloud Build staging bucket
#   .dockerignore  — what `docker build` copies into the image
#
# Without this file gcloud looks for a .gitignore IN THIS DIRECTORY to derive an
# ignore set from. There isn't one — the repo's .gitignore lives at the root, two
# levels up — so the fallback finds nothing and the upload becomes 222 MB (the
# 218 MB .venv) instead of 2.1 MB. .dockerignore would still keep .venv out of
# the image, so the symptom is a slow, fragile upload rather than a broken
# container, which is exactly the kind of thing that goes unnoticed.
#
# Keep the secret patterns first and keep them in sync with .dockerignore: they
# are the reason a stray local .env can never reach the staging bucket.

# Never upload local secrets
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Python artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
venv/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Dev / test files — the suite lives at package root as test_*.py, not tests/
tests/
test_*.py
tools/
fixtures/
seed_backfill.py

# Runtime state written by a pass; regenerated on the instance, never shipped
*.log
stage1_*_usage.json
calibration_log.json

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
